e that condenses the most critical center-panel data (spark chart, line movement summary, top book odds, H2H, status) into a single scrollable column. Line movement is reduced to a single text arrow diagram instead of a full ASCII chart. Live scores are compressed to single-line entries at the bottom-right.\n\n**Strengths:**\n- Fits comfortably in a ~120-character terminal on a standard 1080p or 1440p laptop display\n- The condensed spark chart still communicates the over/under pattern at a glance\n- Single-line live score entries with active player stats give essential context without consuming vertical space\n- The bottom movers/fades summary row compresses the alert panel into two lines\n\n**Considerations:** The line movement chart is simplified to a text representation. If line history granularity matters, this layout should be expanded or the user should switch to Variation 1 on an external display.\n\n---\n\n**Symbol Key used in both mockups:**\n\n| Symbol | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| ● | Live / active feed connected |\n| ○ | Upcoming / not yet live |\n| ▲ | Line moved up / bullish signal |\n| ▼ | Line moved down / bearish signal |\n| → | Line stable / no movement |\n| [+EV] | Positive expected value alert |\n| [FADE] | Negative EV / fade recommendation |\n| ★ | High confidence rating |\n| ██ | Over result (green in color terminal) |\n| ░░ | Under result (red in color terminal) |\n| ◌ | Questionable status |\n| ✗ | Out / not playing |\n\n---\n\nWhich variation would you like to select, or would you prefer to combine elements from both? I can also modify specific panels, adjust column widths, swap out players, or refine any data section."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":100725,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":100725,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CYv8H5KVxBrrW1F